                <pb facs="0107" n="11" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg11"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Long to Superintendent Naval Academy</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Navy Department</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-06-26"><hi rendition="#italic">June 26,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Argentine school ship, at present
                    cruising in these waters, will shortly visit the station under your command. The
                    Department desires you to extend to this ship every courtesy which may be in
                    your power, giving every practicable facility for the inspection of the
                    institution under your command.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John D. Long</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
